      h1('6. Key System Flows'),
      h2('6.1 Seat Booking — Race Condition Prevention'),
      body('The most technically critical flow in the entire system is seat booking. Without proper locking, two passengers booking the last seat simultaneously can both succeed, creating an overbooked trip. PamojaRide solves this with a Postgres RPC function that uses row-level locking:'),
      ...spacer(1),
      callout('book_seats() RPC — how it works', [
        '1. SELECT … FOR UPDATE locks the trip row exclusively',
        '2. Checks seats_available >= requested seats (fails with exception if not)',
        '3. UPDATE trips SET seats_available = seats_available - seats',
        '4. INSERT INTO bookings … RETURNING id',
        '5. All four steps run in one atomic transaction — no partial states possible',
        'Rule: seats_available is NEVER updated from client code. Only this RPC.',
      ], C.amberLight, C.amber, '92400E'),
      ...spacer(1),
      h2('6.2 Trip Lifecycle — Postgres Trigger Notifications'),
