      bullet('Vehicle logbook verification — plate number is cross-referenced against the submitted logbook photo. If the vehicle changes, re-verification is required.', 0),
      bullet('Three-rejection ban — after three KYC rejections, the account is permanently banned and the phone number is blacklisted.', 0),
      ...spacer(1),
      h2('7.2 Operational Layer'),
      bullet('Trust-based seat limits — new drivers can carry at most 2 passengers per trip. Even a successful fraudulent trip causes minimal financial damage before the account is flagged.', 0),
      bullet('Posting bond (Phase 4) — drivers put up a small bond (KES 200–500) when creating a trip, refunded on completion. Fraudulent drivers who ghost before departure lose the bond.', 0),
      bullet('Trip reporting — passengers can flag a trip or driver. Two or more reports on the same trip auto-suspend it pending review.', 0),
      bullet('Progressive trust — drivers cannot jump from 0 to 60 trips overnight. The trust graduation system means a new account has limited blast radius even if it is fraudulent.', 0),
